  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nIssued 209 PM MDT FRI SEP 11 2026\nAs the low pressure system from the weekend moves eastward, \ntroughing continues along the west coast. The troughing will bring \nsouthwesterly flow and eventually strengthen into a closed low that \nrejoins the broader flow later in the week. The period from Monday \nthrough Wednesday will see steadily warming temperatures as the \ntrough and low build. There is a very low chance of showers over \nhigh terrain during this time frame as the closed low blocks the \nbulk of Pacific moisture from reaching the area. Models have shown \nlittle run to run consistency on the track of the closed low as it \nbecomes a longwave trough later in the week. A high amplitude ridge \nfollows closely behind, threatening to continue warming conditions \nwith drier weather if the trough misses us. However, the latest runs \nof long range models show the trough bringing us higher chances for \nprecipitation Thursday and Friday.",
